{
 "title": "Chapter 5: Collapse, and the Man of Steel",
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Chapter 5: Collapse, and the Man of Steel",
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "s06i01",
     "text": "Quick *score* check.",
     "shot": "in_score",
     "type": "HOST",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       2,
       0.5
      ]
     ],
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "s06i02",
     "text": "Land: biggest on Earth. Napoleon: *beaten*.",
     "shot": "in_score",
     "type": "HOST",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "ding",
       "w:Earth",
       0.4
      ],
      [
       "ding",
       "w:beaten",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06i03",
     "text": "People: still *not* enough.",
     "shot": "in_score",
     "type": "HOST",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "boing",
       "w:enough",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06i04",
     "text": "And the next man in charge will try to fix that in the *worst* way possible.",
     "shot": "in_score",
     "type": "HOST"
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b01",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "In 1904, Russia went to war with Japan, expecting an *easy* win.",
     "shot": "c5_japan",
     "date": 1904,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:Japan",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b02",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "It suffered a *humiliating* defeat.",
     "shot": "c5_tsushima",
     "date": 1905,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "thud",
       "w:defeat",
       0.4
      ]
     ],
     "amb": "waves"
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b03",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The *first* time a modern European power had been beaten decisively by an Asian one.",
     "shot": "c5_tsushima",
     "amb": "waves"
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b04",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Then came *World* War I.",
     "shot": "c5_ww1",
     "date": 1914,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       "w:War",
       0.4
      ]
     ],
     "amb": "wind"
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b05",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Millions were sent to the front *without* enough weapons, food, or supplies.",
     "shot": "c5_ww1",
     "amb": "wind"
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b06",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "By early 1917, protests and *bread* riots swept the capital.",
     "shot": "c5_petrograd",
     "date": 1917,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       "w:riots",
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b07",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Soldiers sent to crush them *joined* the crowds.",
     "shot": "c5_petrograd",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:joined",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b08",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Nicholas II *abdicated*, ending the Romanov dynasty.",
     "shot": "c5_abdicate",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "thud",
       "w:abdicated",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b09",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The Bolsheviks, under Lenin, *seized* power.",
     "shot": "c5_lenin",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       "w:seized",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b10",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "In July 1918, Nicholas II, his wife, and their five children were shot in Yekaterinburg.",
     "shot": "c5_ipatiev",
     "date": 1918,
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b11",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "A brutal civil war followed, killing *millions* through fighting, famine, and disease.",
     "shot": "c5_civilwar",
     "date": 1919,
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b12",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "In 1922, the *Soviet* Union was born.",
     "shot": "c5_ussr",
     "date": 1922,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       "w:born",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b13",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "After Lenin died in 1924, a man named Joseph *Stalin* won the struggle to replace him.",
     "shot": "c5_stalin",
     "date": 1924,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:Stalin",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b14",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "He wanted to turn a peasant country into an *industrial* power, fast.",
     "shot": "c5_industry",
     "date": 1929,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "clang",
       "w:fast",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b15",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "And he was willing to pay for it in *lives*.",
     "shot": "c5_industry",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b16",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "He forced millions of peasants onto collective farms and *seized* their grain.",
     "shot": "c5_collective",
     "date": 1930,
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b17",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "In the early 1930s, *famine* killed millions of people in Ukraine,",
     "shot": "map:famine",
     "date": 1932,
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b18",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "*Kazakhstan*, and southern Russia.",
     "shot": "map:famine",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b19",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Then, in 1937 and 1938, came the Great *Terror*.",
     "shot": "c5_terror",
     "date": 1937,
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b20",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The secret police arrested people accused of being *enemies* of the state.",
     "shot": "c5_terror",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b21",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Hundreds of thousands were *shot*.",
     "shot": "c5_terror",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b22",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Millions more passed through the *Gulag* labour camps.",
     "shot": "c5_gulag",
     "date": 1938,
     "quiet": true,
     "amb": "wind"
    },
    {
     "id": "s06i05",
     "text": "Bill number *two*: famine and terror. Millions. Paid by the people the country needed most.",
     "shot": "in_receipt",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b23",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Here is the *contradiction* at the heart of this story.",
     "shot": "c5_contra",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b24",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "For centuries, Russia's central problem was *too* few people for too much land.",
     "shot": "c5_contra",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b25",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "And in the 1930s, its own government *destroyed* millions of them.",
     "shot": "c5_contra",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b26",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "But Stalin wasn't thinking about the future of the *birth* rate.",
     "shot": "c5_thinking",
     "date": 1939
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b27",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "He was thinking about the next *invasion*.",
     "shot": "c5_thinking",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       "w:invasion",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s06b28",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "And in *June* 1941, it came.",
     "shot": "c5_june41",
     "date": 1941,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "thud",
       "w:came",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}